    "shift": "unknown_shift"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A wide slab consisting of two media of refractive indices&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is placed in air as shown in the figure. A ray of light is incident from medium&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is slightly larger than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math>. Take refractive index of air as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Which of the following statement(s) is (are) correct?</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0014_757b21f0698e.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 148px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The light ray enters air if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The light ray is finally reflected back into the medium of refractive index&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The light ray is finally reflected back into the medium of refractive index&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The light ray is reflected back into the medium of refractive index&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0014_01262b8ebfb9.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 215px;\" /></p><p><strong>Option A:</strong> If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From (1) and (2),</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;(given)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;(which is not possible)</p><p>and hence light will reflect back from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>air</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;interface</p><p><strong>Option B:</strong>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>Snell&#39;s law at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Snell&#39;s law at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;(not possible)</p><p>Hence, light might reflect&nbsp;from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>.</p><p><strong>Option C:</strong> If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;(not possible)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Light will reflect back into medium&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><strong>Option D:</strong>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;not possible</p><p>Hence, light will reflect back into the medium.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}